   },
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8c7f2987-f7cf-4059-893b-c17a20fcb308",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##  DFT Methodology & Physics\n",
    "\n",
    "### Computing ΔG‡: The Thermodynamic Framework\n",
    "\n",
    "The activation free energy ΔG‡ is the key quantity connecting theory to experiment (via transition\n",
    "state theory). It is computed from: [4]\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"attachment:34392660-2f79-4642-bfeb-e3488a48ba97.png\" width=\"480\" style=\"display:block; margin:12px 0;\"/>\n",
    "\n",
    "*Figure: The Gibbs free energy of activation formula used in this work.*[4]\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\Delta G^{\\ddagger} = \\Delta E_{\\text{elec}} + \\Delta ZPE + \\Delta H_{\\text{thermal}} - T\\Delta S$$\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### Density Functional Theory (DFT)\n",
    "\n",
    "Density Functional Theory (DFT) is a method used to solve the electronic Schrödinger equation for molecules. Instead of trying to track all electrons interacting with each other directly, DFT simplifies the problem by treating each electron as moving in an effective potential created by all the others.\n",
    "\n",
    "The hardest part of this approach is describing how electrons interact with each other. This is handled by something called the exchange–correlation (XC) functional, which captures all the complicated many-body quantum effects.\n",
    "\n",
    "I am using a wb97XD functional which uses a combination of short and long range Hartree-Fock exchange to better represent the longer M-Cl distances.\n",
    "The basis set: def2svp is able to map the orbitals of each atom using wave equations to model how they bond together or act in the transition state. [5]\n",
    "\n",
    "### Potential Energy Surface (PES) Mapping\n",
    "\n",
    "For each structure, the PES is mapped by finding two stationary points:\n",
    "\n",
    "Reactant geometry (energy minimum):\n",
    "Geometry optimised until forces on all atoms are low.\n",
    "A frequency calculation confirms zero imaginary frequencies which verifies a true minimum.\n",
    "\n",
    "Transition state (first-order saddle point):\n",
    "Located using the Berny algorithm, starting from a geometry with the\n",
    "nucleophile approaching the ipso carbon. The TS is confirmed by exactly **one imaginary frequency**\n",
    "(the reaction coordinate), whose normal mode must show the expected bond-forming and bond-breaking motions —\n",
    "visualised in GaussView to verify the reaction coordinate is correct.\n",
    "\n",
    "Zero-Point Energy (ZPE) correction:\n",
    "Real molecules have vibrational motion even at 0 K so a ZPE correction is necessary.\n",
    "The ZPE for a molecule with 3N−6 vibrational modes is:\n",
    "$$ZPE = \\frac{1}{2}\\sum_{i=1}^{3N-6} h\\nu_i$$\n",
    "This correction is always applied because reactants and transition states have different ZPE values —\n",
    "ignoring it introduces errors of 1–3 kcal/mol in ΔG‡.[5]\n",
    "\n",
    "### The 110+ Structures Computed That will be studied\n",
    "\n",
    "<img src=\"attachment:a6c24f69-a976-4d04-8b72-df7a93b0325c.png\" width=\"700\" style=\"display:block; margin:12px 0;\"/>\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset systematically varies four structural parameters across 110+ completed calculations:\n",
    "- **Scaffold**: biphenyl, naphthalene, anthracene, tetracene (polycyclic aromatic framework)\n",
    "- **Metal**: Fe(CpL), Ru(CpL), Mn(CO)₃ (coordination mode and electronic character)\n",
    "- **Cp ligand substituent L**: unsubstituted Cp, CpCO₂H, CpCl, CpMe (tunes metal electron density via the Cp ring)\n",
    "- **Cl position**: ring 1 through ring 4 (varies M–Cl distance from ~3.5 to >10 Å)\n",
    "\n",
    "This systematic variation allows us to decouple the contributions of each structural variable\n",
    "to ΔG‡ — the core analysis performed in the clustering and regression sections below.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "19609109",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##  Load & Clean Data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "fcb5a060",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv('snar_csv.csv', header=0)\n",
    "df.columns = ['group', 'structure', 'deltaG', 'distance']\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "df['deltaG']    = pd.to_numeric(df['deltaG'],   errors='coerce')\n",
    "df['distance']  = pd.to_numeric(df['distance'], errors='coerce')\n",
    "df['group']     = df['group'].str.strip()\n",
    "df['structure'] = df['structure'].str.strip()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8e0a7cf9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## structure variables coded in\n",
    "\n",
    "Encoded structural variables from the structure naming convention:\n",
    "- **Scaffold**: naphthalene (nap), biphenyl (bip), or polycyclic (anthracene/tetracene)\n",
    "- **Metal**: Fe, Ru, Mn\n",
    "- **Ligand**: Cp substituents (CO₂H, Cl, Me, unsubstituted) or Mn(CO)₃\n",
    "- **Position** & **Ring** from the numerical suffix\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "e19417d6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "name = df['structure'].str.lower()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Scaffold\n",
    "df['scaffold'] = np.where(name.str.startswith('nap'), 0,\n",
    "                 np.where(name.str.startswith('bip'), 1, 2))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Metal\n",
    "df['metal'] = np.where(name.str.contains('_fe_'), 0,\n",
    "              np.where(name.str.contains('_ru_'), 1,\n",
    "              np.where(name.str.contains('_mn_|mn_'), 2, 3)))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ligand / Cp substituent\n",
    "def get_ligand(s):\n",
    "    s = str(s).lower()\n",
    "    for i, lig in enumerate(['cpco2h', 'cpcl', 'cpme', 'cp', '(co)3']):\n",
    "        if lig in s:\n",
    "            return i\n",
    "    return 5\n",
    "\n",
    "df['ligand']   = df['structure'].apply(get_ligand)\n",
    "df['is_prime'] = name.str.contains('prime').astype(int)\n",
    "df['position'] = name.str.extract(r'_(\\d+)').astype(float).fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "metal_map = {0: 'Fe', 1: 'Ru', 2: 'Mn', 3: '—'}\n",
    "lig_map   = {0: 'CpCO₂H', 1: 'CpCl', 2: 'CpMe', 3: 'Cp', 4: 'Mn(CO)₃', 5: 'none'}\n",
    "scaf_map  = {0: 'Naphthalene', 1: 'Biphenyl', 2: 'Polycyclic'}\n",
    "\n",
    "df['metal_name'] = df['metal'].map(metal_map)\n",
    "df['lig_name']   = df['ligand'].map(lig_map)\n",
    "df['scaf_name']  = df['scaffold'].map(scaf_map)\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e0b05c7e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Hierarchical Clustering (Ward Linkage)\n",
    "\n",
    "Cluster all structures using the full feature set:\n",
    "ΔG‡, M–Cl distance, scaffold (encoded), metal (encoded), ligand (encoded), is_prime, position\n",
    "\n",
    "Ward linkage minimizes within-cluster variance at each merge step.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "d00f1fe7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Structures used in clustering: 94\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Drop rows missing deltaG or distance for clustering\n",
    "df_hc = df.dropna(subset=['deltaG', 'distance']).copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "features = ['deltaG', 'distance', 'scaffold', 'metal', 'ligand', 'is_prime', 'position']\n",
    "scaler   = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(df_hc[features])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Structures used in clustering: {len(df_hc)}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "ccd63295",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 2880x960 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Dendrogram \n",
    "Z = linkage(X_scaled, method='ward')\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(24, 8))\n",
    "dendrogram(Z,\n",
    "           labels=df_hc['structure'].values,\n",
    "           leaf_rotation=90,\n",
    "           leaf_font_size=6.5,\n",
    "           color_threshold=8.5,\n",
    "           ax=ax)\n",
    "ax.axhline(y=10, color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=1.5, label='Cut line (k=3)')\n",
    "ax.set_title(\n",
    "    'Hierarchical Clustering Dendrogram — Ward Linkage\\n'\n",
    "    '[ΔG‡, Distance, Scaffold, Metal, Ligand, Prime, Position]',\n",
    "    fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Structure', fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Ward Distance', fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax.legend(fontsize=10)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('ward_dendrogram.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 23,
   "id": "fa0ed43f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Fit AgglomerativeClustering with k=3 \n",
    "k = 3\n",
    "agg = AgglomerativeClustering(n_clusters=k, linkage='ward')\n",
    "df_hc['cluster'] = agg.fit_predict(X_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sort clusters by ascending mean ΔG\n",
    "order   = df_hc.groupby('cluster')['deltaG'].mean().sort_values().index\n",
    "mapping = {old: new for new, old in enumerate(order)}\n",
    "df_hc['cluster'] = df_hc['cluster'].map(mapping)\n",
    "\n",
    "palette_c = {0: '#2ecc71', 1: '#3498db', 2: '#e74c3c'}\n",
    "markers_c  = {0: 'o',       1: 's',       2: '^'}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Cluster descriptions\n",
    "cluster_labels = {}\n",
    "for c in range(k):\n",
    "    sub = df_hc[df_hc['cluster'] == c]\n",
    "    tm  = sub['metal'].mode()[0]\n",
    "    tl  = sub['ligand'].mode()[0]\n",
    "    ts  = sub['scaffold'].mode()[0]\n",
    "    mdG = sub['deltaG'].mean()\n",
    "    cluster_labels[c] = (\n",
    "        f\"C{c}: {metal_map[tm]} / {lig_map[tl]} / {scaf_map[ts]}\"\n",
    "        f\"  (n={len(sub)}, mean ΔG={mdG:.1f} kcal/mol)\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 24,
   "id": "f3cd1220",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x840 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# PCA view of Ward clusters\n",
    "pca    = PCA(n_components=2)\n",
    "coords = pca.fit_transform(X_scaled)\n",
    "df_hc['pca1'] = coords[:, 0]\n",
    "df_hc['pca2'] = coords[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 7))\n",
    "for c in range(k):\n",
    "    grp = df_hc[df_hc['cluster'] == c]\n",
    "    ax.scatter(grp['pca1'], grp['pca2'],\n",
    "               color=palette_c[c], label=cluster_labels[c],\n",
    "               s=80, alpha=0.85, edgecolors='white', linewidths=0.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(f'PC1 ({pca.explained_variance_ratio_[0]*100:.1f}% variance)', fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(f'PC2 ({pca.explained_variance_ratio_[1]*100:.1f}% variance)', fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax.set_title('Hierarchical Clustering — PCA Projection (Ward, k=3)', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('ward_pca.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 25,
   "id": "3faf7f11",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1920x1200 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# ΔG vs Distance scatter (Ward)\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(16, 10))\n",
    "for c in range(k):\n",
    "    grp = df_hc[df_hc['cluster'] == c]\n",
    "    ax.scatter(grp['distance'], grp['deltaG'],\n",
    "               color=palette_c[c], label=cluster_labels[c],\n",
    "               marker=markers_c[c], s=90, alpha=0.85,\n",
    "               edgecolors='white', linewidths=0.6, zorder=3)\n",
    "    for _, row in grp.iterrows():\n",
    "        ax.annotate(row['structure'],\n",
    "                    xy=(row['distance'], row['deltaG']),\n",
    "                    xytext=(5, 5), textcoords='offset points',\n",
    "                    fontsize=10, color=palette_c[c], fontweight='bold',\n",
    "                    bbox=dict(boxstyle='round,pad=0.1', fc='white', ec='none', alpha=0.6))\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('M–Cl Distance (Å)', fontsize=13)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('ΔG‡ (kcal/mol)', fontsize=13)\n",
    "ax.set_title('ΔG‡ vs M–Cl Distance — Hierarchical Clustering (Ward, k=3)',\n",
    "             fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.4)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('ward_scatter.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a3571bff-0a2f-41e0-b33c-42941b9c2639",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "This hierarchical clustering method divides the structures into three distinct groups. The dendrogram starts with each structure being its\n",
    "own group. It combines the structures based on minimal variance until all the structures are combined into one group at the top of the diagram.\n",
    "To divide into groups, the ward distance was chosen to be 10 creating three groups. To varify that these three groups were unique,  \n",
    "the PCA plot is used to put the groups into 2D space from the 7 diminentional space it was in \n",
    "(because of the 7 characteristics it was based on). From there, the scatter plot is made showing the distance between the metal and the\n",
    "chlorine compared to the deltaG in kcal/mol. The best performing group is the green one which contains all the biphenyl ring1 stuctures as well\n",
    "as the naptholene ring1 and ring2 structures. Overall, these are the structures with the shortest M-Cl distance. \n",
    "The second best group is the blue group. This group contains all the tetracene and athrocene structures. This group is interesting because\n",
    "as the M-Cl distance increases, the deltaG increases at a reduced rate compared to the other structures. \n",
    " The worst performig group is the red group. These are the biphenyl ring2 structures. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ac19d957",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## K-Means Clustering (k=3)\n",
    "\n",
    "K-Means partitions structures by minimizing within-cluster sum of squared distances to centroids.\n",
    "We compare results with the hierarchical approach to validate robustness of cluster assignments.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 26,
   "id": "5f8a8ff0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 960x600 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Elbow method \n",
    "# Use imputed ΔG for rows missing values (so we keep the full dataset)\n",
    "df_km = df.copy()\n",
    "df_km['deltaG_f']   = df_km['deltaG'].fillna(df_km['deltaG'].mean())\n",
    "df_km['distance_f'] = df_km['distance'].fillna(df_km['distance'].mean())\n",
    "\n",
    "features_km = ['deltaG_f', 'distance_f', 'scaffold', 'metal', 'ligand', 'is_prime', 'position']\n",
    "scaler_km   = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_km        = scaler_km.fit_transform(df_km[features_km])\n",
    "\n",
    "inertias = [KMeans(n_clusters=k, random_state=42, n_init=10).fit(X_km).inertia_\n",
    "            for k in range(1, 11)]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "ax.plot(range(1, 11), inertias, 'bo-', markersize=8)\n",
    "ax.axvline(3, color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=1.5, label='k=3 (selected)')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel('Number of clusters (k)', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel('Inertia (within-cluster SS)', fontsize=12)\n",
    "ax.set_title('Elbow Method for Optimal k', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.legend(fontsize=11)\n",
    "ax.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('kmeans_elbow.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
