  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2d2a7092",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "##  Clustering Results\n",
    "**K-means**\n",
    "\n",
    "The grouping for the K-means uses a different algorithm where the groups are decided based on their distance from the centroids. The PCA plot shows us this in 2D space. Despite this, the groupings are identical to the hierarchical method varifying the results.\n",
    "\n",
    "**overall findings for Tau arylation:**\n",
    "\n",
    "- Mn(CO)₃ on biphenyl/naphthalene consistently gives the lowest ΔG‡ (~12–14 kcal/mol).\n",
    "  Mn(CO)₃ is a stronger π-acid than Fe(Cp) or Ru(Cp) because the three CO ligands are strong\n",
    "  trans-influence σ-donors that push electron density back onto the metal, making it more\n",
    "  electron-withdrawing from the ring. This gives the most activated ipso carbon.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Fe-Cp and Ru-Cp polycyclics span the widest ΔG‡ range (~14–35 kcal/mol),\n",
    "  reflecting strong position-dependence across rings 1–4.\n",
    "\n",
    "- M–Cl distance < 3.7 Å is the clearest structural predictor of low-barrier reactivity.\n",
    "  These are exclusively ring-1 attacks where the Cl leaving group sits directly in the\n",
    "  coordination sphere of the metal.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4df84758",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Additional Advanced Statistical Modeling**\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Linear Regression: ΔG‡ vs. M–Cl Distance:\n",
    "From the results, the M-Cl distance is a large contributer to the activation energy. A linear regression is done to see if that alone is a good predictive model. \n",
    "It can be extended to a multivariate regression to understand if a combination of factors is a better predicitive model.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Least-squares fit regression against structure descriptors.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Correlated fits and interdependency testing. This is done\n",
    "because several factors are not independent like the (CO)3 on Mn complexes\n",
    "\n",
    "4. uncertainty propagation"
   ]
